From 427b538f72820fcc88cdf2b0a25f385644a21789 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: drh <>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 13:07:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix a possible OOB write in the recover extension given a
 corrupt schema.  [bugs:/info/2026-10-25T12:08:19Z|Bug 2026-10-25T12:08:19Z].

[Hades: backport to 3.54.1 from branch-3.54. The release is the amalgamation, so the change is made where ext/recover/sqlite3recover.c in shell.c. Not carried: ext/recover/recovercorrupt4.test (tests of the source tree).]

FossilOrigin-Name: 37963c3869640f9857dd4edf5e26fdca336ec71d8b1cf188507cab5fad91f681
Upstream: https://sqlite.org/src/info/37963c3869640f9857dd4edf5e26fdca336ec71d8b1cf188507cab5fad91f681
---
 shell.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/shell.c b/shell.c
index 4be10a2..98f2d29 100644
--- a/shell.c
+++ b/shell.c
@@ -23196,7 +23196,7 @@ static void recoverAddTable(
       int iField = sqlite3_column_int(pStmt, 0);
       int iCol = sqlite3_column_int(pStmt, 1);
 
-      assert( iCol<pNew->nCol );
+      if( iCol>=pNew->nCol ) break;
       pNew->aCol[iCol].iField = iField;
 
       pNew->bIntkey = 0;
